Hmm, the disuasion condition in MODELO §2.5 is `κ·q·(ρ_ret I T_v + c_r + I M) > V/N` — this says the bribe per recruited farmer (the loss they suffer times the probability they leave evidence and it lands) exceeds the attacker's gain per recruited farmer V/N. Wait no: soborno_necesario = κ q pérdida must be > V/N to deter? Actually if the attacker must pay the recruited more than V/N (his gain per recruit), recruiting is unprofitable. Wait but that's the compensation to the recruit. Hmm.

Actually there's a subtlety: `V/N` is the value of the attack per recruited farmer? V is "valor del ataque por reclutado". So attacker gains V per recruited. To recruit, they must compensate the recruit for expected loss `κ q pérdida` (the recruit might get slashed if evidence lands). For the recruitment to be unprofitable to the attacker, the compensation > gain.

But wait, that doesn't involve the attacker's actual gain being "V" total or per recruited. V is defined as "valor del ataque por reclutado (lo que gana con la trampa)". So the total attack value scales with reclutados. Hmm.

Actually the order's (a) says: "hace que reclutar el espacio que falta para ganar una rama privada cueste más que lo que el atacante gana". So cost of recruiting > gain.

