Wait, the bisection is `lo, hi = F, min(Tv_max, 1e12)`. If Tv_max=1141, then hi=1141. Bisection finds hi with A_ok(hi). If A_ok(1141) is false, it wouldn't bisect (we return early if `!A_ok(Tv_max)`). So A_ok(Tv_max) must be true. Hmm. But I computed cost=0. Let me recheck: maybe `B_de(esc.dist, x)` for ParetoDist uses `B_par(d::ParetoDist, x)`. And `B_par` for alpha>2 uses F_max=Inf. With x=8.76e-6, fmin=1e-8: (fmin/x)^{0.5} = (1e-8/8.76e-6)^{0.5} = (0.0011416)^{0.5}=0.0338. 1-0.0338=0.966. Yes.

